		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Compound child with static bounds not working]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=3233#p3233"><![CDATA[
When both children have static bounds they do not collide, but if only one of the colliding children use static the collision works fine. I was using a non default mesh, not the one in this file.<br> This example will show what I'm talking about. after playing once, change only one of the children to box or convex and it works fine. Only static to static don't work.<br><br><a href="http://appolonius1978.googlepages.com/compound_child_static_bounds.blend" class="postlink">http://appolonius1978.googlepages.com/c ... unds.blend</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1343">Appolonius</a> — Tue Jan 16, 2007 5:21 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
